bibliothecaire — the ecosystem's librarian. Zach-directed /ideate session
2026-07-26; full vision + milestone chain in .claude/FOCUS.md same date
(read that entry before scaffolding — it records four explicit decisions).

Two wings, one project:
(a) operations/cybernetics knowledge base seeded from realisateur's
    UNIVERSE.md — research the principles it leans on and extend to the
    named themes: what makes closed loops work, stigmergy (Grassé),
    theories of the firm (Coase), holons (Koestler), plus the already-cited
    Ashby (An Introduction to Cybernetics), Beer/VSM, Laozi. Deliverable of
    the FIRST research pass: sourced quotes with real attribution,
    published as a consumable quotes file (format open — design it so
    crt's idle-bait rotation can read it; see crt FOCUS.md 2026-07-26
    (realisateur) entry for the consumer's side). This KB is intended to
    become a core philosophical resource for realisateur.
(b) crt's book-catalog knowledge wing (contents/relationships/citations/
    further-reading) — merged in from crt's formerly-parked catalog split.
    LATER milestone, not the first pass: greenfield, never forks crt's
    scan/grade/STT code, shares at most books.db's data.

Scaffolding instructions:
- Register in _paced.conf at LOW weight — still-forming dream per /ideate
  §4.6 and UNIVERSE.md's convergence test (three arrivals in three
  shapes). The first case (quote extraction) is concrete; the whole is not.
- Consumers read the published quotes file; they never import code.
- Name is settled: this project owns "bibliothecaire". The unrelated
  page-92 idea is now quatre-vingt-douze.idea. Check the queued NAMES.md
  item before scaffolding anything else with a French noun.
